        1927,
        2758
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Section 1. There is established the Council on Consumer Affairs which shall consist of the chief officer of each of the following departments and agencies of the City of New York: Community Development Agency, Council Against Poverty, Health Services Administration, Law Department, Department of Licenses, Department of Markets and the Department of Welfare. The Mayor shall appoint the Chairman and the Secretary of the Council of Consumer Affairs and the Council shall meet at the call of the Chairman.",
